From ffac562a8a502dc98c2542751090ef105dfd89f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:04:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: U2214 DAC data buffer, START events, EMPTY and DMA

The PIC32CM DAC's buffered path as PIC32CM MC00 silicon showed it
(firmware/hello APP=dacprobe..dacprobe3, checked by dacbuf):

- Every enable sets INTFLAG.EMPTY, whatever DATABUF holds; a DATA or
  DATABUF write clears it.
- A DATABUF write fills the buffer; SYNCBUSY.DATA and DATABUF read 1
  until a START event moves it into DATA, and writes meanwhile are
  dropped (the data sheet's rule for writes during synchronization).
- A START event ("start-event-in", EVCTRL.STARTEI, rising edge or
  falling with INVEI) moves a full DATABUF; without dithering every
  START sets EMPTY, and one finding DATABUF empty sets UNDERRUN too.
- CTRLB.DITHER: the 14-bit value, output as its average; EMPTY comes
  every 16th START from the enable and UNDERRUN only on the START that
  opens a group of 16, while a full DATABUF moves at any START.
- Setting EMPTY pulses "empty-event" (EVCTRL.EMPTYEO) and is the EMPTY
  DMA request: the SoC wires DMAC_ID_EMPTY as a level trigger on
  INTFLAG, and the DAC kicks the DMAC. All PIC32CM DMA triggers are
  wired now.

The overlay gives SYNCBUSY a read hook. qtest pic32cm-dac-test: EMPTY
at the enable, DATABUF and START, INVEI, dithering, DMA.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
